¶ The minor @@R1@@
>>>
<<<
@@R1@@
===
keys which have their names in parentheses, namely *E₁*♭, *B₁*♭, *F₁*, *C₁*, *G₁*, *D₁*, have a true minor Seventh, but too high a leading tone. [Their dominant chord has an impossible Pythagorean major Third.] For the six keys marked with (⁎), the arrangement@@R1@@
>>>
<<<
@@R1@@
===
 of the stops is the same both for major and minor.†

In order to have a complete series of tonics, each with a perfect major and minor form it would be necessary to cut off *a₁*♭, *e₁*♭, *b₁*♭, *f₁*, *c₁*, *g₁*, from the other notes, and to allow them to be @@R1@@
>>>
<<<
@@R1@@
===
replaced when needed by *g*♯, *d*♯, *a*♯, *e*♯, *b*♯, and *f*♯♯, by means of a fifth stop. We should thus have 30 tones to the octave. By drawing out this stop we should have the following system of keys:—

